    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμετά-δοτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not imparting, sharing,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				145
			</span></i>: abs., <i>niggardly,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span> Nic.Dam.<i><span class="en">
				p.144b28
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; of persons, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοινωνητικοί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epict.
				<u>Sent.</u>
				6
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως, ζῆν</span> live <i>without giving to
				any one,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.525d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>not imparted, secret,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφήγησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Vett.Val.
					331.6
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Par.</u>
				1.256
			</span></i>.</div>
